1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"library--effort-and-time-tracking","kind":"library-article","route":"/roadmap/library/effort-and-time-tracking","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/library/effort-and-time-tracking","sourceHash":"c586ab457e8f74659e656da3d508391895015dc4c0f054a922fd777905ae20c6","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T16:52:53.277Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"Effort and Time Tracking","zh":"投入与时间追踪"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Tracking how much time you spend learning — and what you spend it on — is one of the simplest things you can do to improve your results. In Refold's experience with clients, tracking effort is directly correlated with success.","zh":"记录自己花了多少时间学习，以及时间具体花在了什么活动上，是改善学习成果最简单的方法之一。根据 Refold 服务学员的经验，追踪投入程度与学习成功直接相关。"}},{"id":"why-track","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Why Track","zh":"为什么要追踪"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"<strong>Accountability:</strong> It's harder to skip a day when you're looking at a tracker","zh":"<strong>自我督促：</strong>当你每天都要面对追踪记录时，就不那么容易偷懒一天"},{"en":"<strong>Awareness:</strong> You discover where your time actually goes (vs. where you think it goes)","zh":"<strong>了解实情：</strong>你会发现自己的时间实际上花在了哪里，而不是你以为花在了哪里"},{"en":"<strong>Progress visibility:</strong> Hours accumulate slowly day by day, but tracking makes the total visible","zh":"<strong>看见进展：</strong>每天的学习时长增长得很慢，但追踪记录能让你看到累计总量"},{"en":"<strong>Balance checking:</strong> Are you spending enough time on interactive immersion? Too much on vocab study? Tracking reveals imbalances.","zh":"<strong>检查平衡：</strong>你花在互动式沉浸上的时间够吗？词汇学习是否过多？追踪记录可以揭示这些失衡。"},{"en":"<strong>Motivation:</strong> Seeing consistent effort over weeks and months is deeply motivating","zh":"<strong>保持动力：</strong>看到自己数周乃至数月始终坚持投入，会带来强大的动力"}]},{"id":"what-to-track","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"What to Track","zh":"追踪哪些内容"}},{"id":"segment-0005","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"At minimum, track the number of minutes you spend learning each day. Better yet, tag your time by activity type (priming, interactive, freeflow, output) so you can check whether your balance matches the recommendations for your current phase.","zh":"至少要记录自己每天学习了多少分钟。更理想的做法是按照活动类型为时间添加标签（预热、互动式沉浸、自由流沉浸、输出），这样就能检查各类活动的时间分配是否符合当前阶段的建议。"}},{"id":"tools","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Tools","zh":"工具"}},{"id":"segment-0007","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The <a href=\"https://refold.link/webapp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Refold App</a> has built-in tracking. You can also use a simple spreadsheet, a different habit tracking app, or even a paper tally. The tool doesn't matter — consistency matters. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-refold-app\">The Refold App</a>","zh":"<a href=\"https://refold.link/webapp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Refold App</a> 内置了追踪功能。你也可以使用简单的电子表格、其他习惯追踪应用，甚至在纸上记数。用什么工具并不重要，坚持记录才重要。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/the-refold-app\">Refold App</a>"}},{"id":"tips","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Tips","zh":"小贴士"}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Don't let tracking become a source of stress. A rough estimate is better than nothing.","zh":"不要让追踪记录成为压力来源。粗略估算也好过完全不记录。"},{"en":"Aim for an 80%+ \"hit rate\" (days where you hit your goal) rather than a perfect streak. <a href=\"/roadmap/library/habit-health\">Habit Health</a>","zh":"与其追求从不间断的完美连续记录，不如争取达到 80% 以上的“达标率”（即完成目标的天数比例）。<a href=\"/roadmap/library/habit-health\">习惯健康度</a>"},{"en":"Review your tracking weekly to spot trends and adjust.","zh":"每周回顾一次追踪记录，找出趋势并作出调整。"}]}],"cards":[]}}]
